st weakness the belief that  they're invincible  although they are outnumbered arminius  plans to exploit this belief of  invincibility  by splitting the army up in the forest  and launching an ambush  think of it as a giant snake hacked into  smaller more manageable parts  but the peace between the germanic  tribes is frail before the battle is to  take place hadkin  reich of the chattan bows out after this  nilda denies him she was promised to him  by sagestus as his bride  to unite their tribes but he's a piece  of [ __ ] and this nelda is now married to  armenius a marriage that started as one  of convenience  a way for armenius to gain the trust of  the tribe since he's still considered  a roman outsider with hadkins men no  longer in the fight the other reichs bow  out but it's up to thessnelda who they  believe is a seer handpicked by the gods  to rally them for much of the season  this nilda has had a strange  relationship with the gods  often calling on them for help and  sacrificing her blood in the process  she claims to have dreams which predict  the future and she tells the men that  she's seen the outcome of the battle  a glorious victory over the romans but  to really  prove to the men she means business she  cuts her eyes  sacrificing it like their god wolten did  to his own eye to see the future now  it's never really explained whether her  eyesight in this eye is gone for good  she wears an eye patch during the battle  but later when talking to armenia she  says she's fine so we'll have to put a  pin in that one for now  this idea of sacrificing to the gods has  major implications for next season  as falquin promises his firstborn child  in exchange for the power to defeat  varys in one of the biggest reveals of  the episode runa the oracle  tells thus nelda that she's been with  child for some time  and the father isn't who she thinks it  is meaning the father is likely  fulquin and not her husband armenius and  with fulquin having promised his  f